  "file": "docs/OPERATIONS.md",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "An operator sees all provider slots occupied and consults the troubleshooting table. They incorrectly expect the run to stop for human intervention while it is actually waiting for a slot.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"${TMPDIR%/}\"/limitless-adjudication.*/probe.ts",
    "output": "F2 while busy: {\"status\":\"running\",\"settled\":false,\"calls\":0,\"wait\":\"waiting for alpha slot (0 ahead), up to unbounded\"}\nF2 after release: {\"settled\":true,\"calls\":1}"
   },
   "evidence": "The offline probe saturated a fake provider, invoked RunContext.invoke, observed the pending invocation, then released the slot. At head, src/pipeline/context.ts:525\u2013539 throws NoCapacityError when no eligible target exists; lines 541\u2013578 instead wait for admission when providers are busy. Engine lines 275 and 345 map NoCapacityError to needs_human. Waiting can eventually exhaust an invocation deadline, but contention does not immediately end the run. OPERATIONS states `No provider capacity ends a run needs_human` without this distinction. Base instead listed `concurrency limit, or no provider available` as queued causes; the inaccurate blanket statement is new."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "An operator reads that no provider capacity ends a run as needs_human. When every eligible provider is just busy, the run actually stays running and waits for a slot, so the operator may think something is wrong, or wrongly expect the run to have ended.",
   "reproduction": "unreproduced: docs-only claim; checked by reading the routing code in src/pipeline/context.ts",
   "evidence": "At head, the OPERATIONS.md troubleshooting row says: \"No provider capacity ends a run `needs_human`, rather than leaving it queued.\" In context.ts (~525-539), `if (!target) { ... throw new NoCapacityError(...) }` applies only when no candidate is eligible. engine.ts:275 maps NoCapacityError to needs_human. When candidates exist but are busy, context.ts (~541-578) waits for a slot instead (`// With no alternative left, contention waits until a slot opens or the invocation deadline`, `tracker.acquire/acquireFirst`, log `waiting for ${provider} slot`). So 'no capacity \u2192 needs_human' is true for routing exhaustion but not for slot contention. The part about runs not staying `queued` is correct."
  }
